G37.def:
from 40; to make holy, i.e. (ceremonially) purify or consecrate;
(mentally) to venerate:--hallow, be holy, sanctify.

see GREEK for 40

G47.def:
from 53; cleanliness (the quality), i.e. (specially)
chastity:--purity.

see GREEK for 53

G49.def:
from 48; a cleansing (the act), i.e. (ceremonially)
lustration:--purification.

see GREEK for 48

G53.def:
from the same as 40; properly, clean, i.e. (figuratively) innocent,
modest, perfect:--chaste, clean, pure.

see GREEK for 40

G54.def:
from 53; cleanness (the state), i.e. (figuratively)
blamelessness:--pureness.

see GREEK for 53

G59.def:
from 58; properly, to go to market, i.e. (by implication) to purchase;
specially, to redeem:--buy, redeem.

see GREEK for 58

G68.def:
from 71; a field (as a drive for cattle); genitive case, the country;
specially, a farm, i.e. hamlet:--country, farm, piece of ground, land.

see GREEK for 71

G74.def:
from 73; a struggle (properly, the state), i.e. (figuratively)
anguish:--agony.

see GREEK for 73

G104.def:
from an obsolete primary noun (apparently meaning continued duration);
"ever,"by qualification regularly; by implication, earnestly;
--always, ever.

G111.def:
from 1 (as a negative particle) and a derivative of themis (statute;
from the base of 5087); illegal; by implication,
flagitious:--abominable, unlawful thing.

see GREEK for 1

see GREEK for 5087

G139.def:
from 138; properly, a choice, i.e. (specially) a party or (abstractly)
disunion:--heresy (which is the Greek word itself), sect.

see GREEK for 138

G152.def:
from 153; shame or disgrace (abstractly or concretely):--dishonesty,
shame.

see GREEK for 153

G155.def:
from 154; a thing asked or (abstractly) an asking:--petition, request,
required.

see GREEK for 154

G189.def:
from 191; hearing (the act, the sense or the thing heard):--audience,
ear, fame, which ye heard, hearing, preached, report, rumor.

see GREEK for 191

G211.def:
neuter of alabastros (of uncertain derivation), the name of a stone;
properly, an "alabaster" box, i.e. (by extension) a perfume vase (of
any material):--(alabaster) box.

G212.def:
from 213; braggadocio, i.e. (by implication)
self-confidence:--boasting, pride.

see GREEK for 213

G316.def:
from 318; necessary; by implication, close (of kin):--near, necessary,
necessity, needful.

see GREEK for 318

G376.def:
from 303 (in the sense of intensity) and peros (maimed);
crippled:--maimed.

see GREEK for 303

G395.def:
from 393; a rising of light, i.e. dawn (figuratively); by implication,
the east (also in plural):--dayspring, east, rising.

see GREEK for 393

G403.def:
from 404; properly, a recovery of breath, i.e. (figuratively)
revival:--revival.

see GREEK for 404

G417.def:
from the base of 109; wind; (plural) by implication, (the four)
quarters (of the earth):--wind.

see GREEK for 109

G431.def:
from 1 (as a particle of union) and an obsolete nepos (a brood);
properly, akin, i.e. (specially) a cousin:--sister's son.

see GREEK for 1

G442.def:
from 444; human:--human, common to man, man(-kind), (man-)kind, men's,
after the manner of men.

see GREEK for 444

G458.def:
from 459; illegality, i.e. violation of law or (genitive case)
wickedness:--iniquity, X transgress(-ion of) the law, unrighteousness.

see GREEK for 459

G485.def:
from a derivative of 483; dispute, disobedience:--contradiction,
gainsaying, strife.

see GREEK for 483

G509.def:
from 507; from above; by analogy, from the first; by implication,
anew:--from above, again, from the beginning (very first), the top.

see GREEK for 507

G515.def:
from 514; to deem entitled or fit:--desire, think good, count (think)
worthy.

see GREEK for 514

G543.def:
from 545; disbelief (obstinate and rebellious):--disobedience,
unbelief.

see GREEK for 545

G544.def:
from 545; to disbelieve (wilfully and perversely):--not believe,
disobedient, obey not, unbelieving.

see GREEK for 545

G650.def:
from 575 and stereo (to deprive); to despoil:--defraud, destitute,
kept back by fraud.

see GREEK for 575

G664.def:
adverb from a derivative of a comparative of 575 and temno (to cut);
abruptly, i.e. peremptorily:--sharply(-ness).

see GREEK for 575

G701.def:
from 700; agreeable; by implication, fit:--(things that) please(-ing),
reason.

see GREEK for 700

G759.def:
from 142 (in the sense of sending off scent); an aromatic:--(sweet)
spice.

see GREEK for 142

G763.def:
from 765; impiety, i.e. (by implication)
wickedness:--ungodly(-liness).

see GREEK for 765

G764.def:
from 765; to be (by implied act) impious or wicked:--commit (live,
that after should live) ungodly.

see GREEK for 765

G769.def:
from 772; feebleness (of mind or body); by implication, malady;
morally, frailty:--disease, infirmity, sickness, weakness.

see GREEK for 772

G819.def:
from 820; infamy, i.e. (subjectively) comparative indignity,
(objectively) disgrace:--dishonour, reproach, shame, vile.

see GREEK for 820

G859.def:
from 863; freedom; (figuratively) pardon:--deliverance, forgiveness,
liberty, remission.

see GREEK for 863

G861.def:
from 862; incorruptibility; genitive, unending existence;
(figuratively) genuineness:--immortality, incorruption, sincerity.

see GREEK for 862

G867.def:
from 864; properly, arrival, i.e. (by implication)
departure:--departing.

see GREEK for 864

G877.def:
from 878; senselessness, i.e. (euphemistically) egotism; (morally)
recklessness:--folly, foolishly(-ness).

see GREEK for 878

G899.def:
from the same as 901; profundity, i.e. (by implication) extent;
(figuratively) mystery:--deep(-ness, things), depth.

see GREEK for 901

G926.def:
from the same as 922; weighty, i.e. (fig) burdensome,
grave:--grievous, heavy, weightier.

see GREEK for 922

G970.def:
probably akin to 970 (through the idea of vital activity);
force:--violence.

see GREEK for 970

G987.def:
from 989; to vilify; specially, to speak impiously:--(speak)
blaspheme(-er, -mously, -my), defame, rail on, revile, speak evil.

see GREEK for 989

G990.def:
from 991; vision (properly concrete; by implication,
abstract):--seeing.

see GREEK for 991
